<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Richman et al. (1975) & Tallinen et al. (2014, 2016) neo-Hookean constrained cortical expansion and sulcal creasing instability, with a Pass 3 3D hemispheric Swift-Hohenberg surface surrogate — Code-to-model traceability: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module header maps Laws 1-6 to their papers and to the 6 Lean theorems by name (L34-74); every Pass 3 function carries a docstring naming the equation and source (GSH Eq. 1 of Stoop 2015 at L526-538, Lyapunov functional at L507-509, Fischl & Dale thickness range, honeycomb bound), the honesty note (L376-388) states exactly what is and is not emergent, and the math-KG YAML registers equations 4-6 with single-range `code_locus` pins. Deductions: the GI growth law is written with exponent 0.85 in Panel C and the GIF (L1175, L1532) but 0.88 in the solver (L267) — the plotted curve is not the curve the solver uses (-5); constants 1.603 / 0.88 / 0.22 / 0.65 / 0.18 / 2.8 / 4.2 in the 2D solver (L265-288) are uncited (-5); eps_scale 0.5 and g2 0.35 are documented but not derived (-3); the Y- junction raster ignores the polar caps (|lat| > 60 deg) and the longitude wrap of `ndi.label`, which is not stated in the docstring (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py L1175–L1175: Panel C GI law uses exponent 0.85 while the solver (L267) uses 0.88 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py#L1175-L1175>",
        "1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py L1532–L1532: GIF GI curve also uses exponent 0.85 — inconsistent with the solver <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py#L1532-L1532>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Richman et al. (1975) & Tallinen et al. (2014, 2016) neo-Hookean constrained cortical expansion and sulcal creasing instability, with a Pass 3 3D hemispheric Swift-Hohenberg surface surrogate — Model fidelity to source: 78/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Laws 1-3 (growth excess Delta_g = max(0, g - g_c), lambda = 2 pi h (mu_c / 3 mu_s)^(1/3), GI = 1 + 2 N d / P_hull; L162-189) are Richman's and Zilles's and are machine-checked. The Pass 3 GSH surrogate (L515-576) is a recognised reduced model for film-on-curved-substrate wrinkling (Stoop 2015), its Lyapunov energy (L506-512) decreases in every supercritical stage, its uniform mode is damped and its subcritical null is exact; the cotangent Laplace-Beltrami operator passes kernel, area and l = 1 eigenvalue checks (self-test #9). Deductions: the 2D coronal \"neo-Hookean\" solver is not a buckling model — n_sulci_target = round(P_hull / lambda_theory) (L253), gi_target = 1 + 1.603 dg^0.88 thinness_boost (L266-267) and the cusp profile u_eq (L272-276) are prescribed, and the energy (L290-314) penalises deviation from u_eq, so L-BFGS-B denoises a target rather than selecting a mode (-10); the 3D surrogate imposes k_c(x) and imports depth from the 2D solver (L735-736), so neither wavelength nor amplitude is emergent in 3D and the requested volumetric FEM is absent (-6); the Lissencephaly control has g = 1.14 < g_c so h = 6.5 mm is never exercised — Richman's thick-cortex prediction (longer wavelength) is not tested (-3); eps_scale and g2_curvature_coeff are unsourced (-3); the honesty note (L376-388) and the Lean coverage of all 6 laws prevent a larger deduction." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py L253–L276: 2D solver prescribes n_sulci_target from P_hull/lambda_theory, gi_target from unsourced constants 1.603/0.88/0.22 and a cusp profile u_eq before minimisation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py#L253-L276>",
        "1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py L290–L314: Energy is a penalty on (u - u_eq) plus bending/slope differences from u_eq: L-BFGS-B relaxes toward the prescribed profile <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py#L290-L314>",
        "1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py L735–L736: 3D crease-wall GI uses mean_sulcal_depth_mm from the 2D shell of the same stage — depth is not emergent in 3D <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py#L735-L736>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Richman et al. (1975) & Tallinen et al. (2014, 2016) neo-Hookean constrained cortical expansion and sulcal creasing instability, with a Pass 3 3D hemispheric Swift-Hohenberg surface surrogate — Morphometric validation: 68/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1572-1743) returns 15 reference-anchored measurements, 6 new in Pass 3 (L1682-1743) with explicit caveats in their `note` fields. Credited: the GW22 subcritical null is exact (0 junctions, GI_3D = 1), Y-junction count rises 0 -> 21 -> 122 and sulcal components fall 178 -> 40 across GW26 -> GW38 (a genuinely emergent topological result), GI_3D 2.604 vs 2.56, and the gradient sweep reports slope, SE, r and RMSE. Deductions: measurements #1, #3 and #9 (L1592-1621, L1672-1681) compare the Richman formula with `lambda_obs_mm` values that are themselves 4.3633 h in the JSON (L41-276), so r = 1.0000 / alpha = 0.9993 / lambda/h = 4.3642 are formula-vs-formula (-12); measurements #4, #5 and #7 (L1622-1661) report the prescribed 2D targets (lambda_sim 11.20 = P_hull / round(P_hull / lambda_theory), GI_sim = gi_target, 85/28 = the empirical counts), so their agreement is by construction (-8); #10 and #14 are consistency checks because k_c(x) is imposed (stated in the notes) (-3); #12 and #15 have only a mathematical upper bound (honeycomb 2.31) and a \">1\" lower bound as references, with no empirical fetal sulcal-graph value (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py L1592–L1621: Measurements #1 and #3 regress formula wavelengths against lambda_obs_mm that are formula-generated in the reference JSON (circular r = 1.0000) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py#L1592-L1621>",
        "1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py L1622–L1661: Measurements #4, #5, #7 report lambda_sim, GI_sim and sulcus counts that equal the prescribed targets of the 2D solver <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py#L1622-L1661>",
        "datasets/cortical_gyrification_folding/cortical_gyrification_folding_reference.json L41–L276: Every lambda_obs_mm equals 4.3633 * h_cortex_mm (e.g. GW26 1.65 -> 7.20, mouse 0.88 -> 3.84); no per-value figure/table provenance <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/datasets/cortical_gyrification_folding/cortical_gyrification_folding_reference.json#L41-L276>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-11-species-mammalian-gyrification-index-scaling-correlation-tallinen-2014-mota-2015>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-11-species-mammalian-sulcal-wavelength-scaling-correlation-richman-1975-tallinen-2014>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-3d-crease-wall-gyrification-index-gi-3d-1-l-zero-d-mean-a-hull-at-gw38-hemispheric-gsh-planform>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-3d-gsh-subcritical-null-y-junctions-and-gi-3d-at-gw22-g-1-12-g-c>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-3d-gsh-sulcal-network-percolation-across-ontogeny-largest-sulcal-component-fraction-gw38-gw26>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-3d-hemispheric-gsh-surface-gw38-emergent-sulcal-wavelength-lambda-3d-cotangent-laplace-beltrami-10242-nodes>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-3d-sulcal-y-junction-density-at-gw38-labyrinth-trivalent-skeleton-nodes-per-lambda-2-lat-60-deg>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-coronal-human-brain-specimen-segmented-gyrification-index-gi-specimen-cerebral-cortex-gyri-specimen-jpg>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-cross-species-log-log-power-law-exponent-alpha-lambda-h-alpha>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-human-gw38-l-bfgs-b-relaxed-neo-hookean-shell-gyrification-index-gi-sim>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-human-gw38-l-bfgs-b-relaxed-neo-hookean-shell-sulcal-wavelength-lambda-sim>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-polymicrogyria-vs-normogyria-sulcus-frequency-modulation-ratio-richman-et-al-1975>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-regional-thickness-gradient-sweep-emergent-anterior-posterior-wavelength-ratio-at-beta-0-3-h-2-08-3-12-mm>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-universal-dimensionless-sulcal-wavelength-to-thickness-invariant-lambda-h-across-11-mammals>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-zero-growth-lissencephaly-negative-control-gyrification-index-g-g-c-vs-gw38>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-morphometric-validation-2> ;
