<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Richman et al. (1975) & Tallinen et al. (2014, 2016) neo-Hookean constrained cortical expansion and sulcal creasing instability, with a Pass 3 3D hemispheric Swift-Hohenberg surface surrogate — Morphological realism / specimen match: 82/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The SHA-256-locked coronal specimen is segmented into gray ribbon, white core, hull and 52 sulcal troughs (L964-1058; GI_specimen 2.8115, CV 0.32) and shown in Panel E; the new 3D figure (`render_surface_3d_figure`, L1352-1482) shows a GW26 dimple field becoming a GW38 labyrinth with Y-junctions on an ellipsoidal hemisphere, which is the qualitative Stoop/Tallinen picture, and GI_3D 2.604 lies within 2% of Zilles's 2.56. Deductions: the specimen is a single coronal section compared with a whole-hemisphere mean (-3); P_pial is approximated as P_hull + 2 sum(depths) from a distance transform rather than traced (L1025-1026), and segmentation thresholds (0.86, 0.08, 14 px, 52nd and 76th percentiles, 62 px band) are untraced tuning constants with a hard-coded fallback spacing [34, 36, 35] (L991-1018, L1034) (-5); the 3D geometry is an ad-hoc ellipsoid, not an MRI template, and no fetal MRI/sulcal-graph image is compared against the 3D planform (-6); the 11-species GI match (r = 0.9985) rests on the prescribed 2D solver (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py L991–L1034: Untraced thresholds 0.86/0.08/14 px/52nd/76th percentile/62 px band and fallback spacings [34, 36, 35]; P_pial approximated from distance-transform depths <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py#L991-L1034>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-specimen-match-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-specimen-match-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-specimen-match-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-specimen-match-5> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

